## Next Steps for the User

To complete the Vercel Web Analytics setup:

1. **Enable Analytics in Vercel Dashboard**
   - Navigate to your project's Analytics section
   - Click the "Enable" button
   - This adds the required routes at `/_vercel/insights/*`

2. **Deploy to Vercel**
   - Run `vercel deploy` or push to your connected Git repository
   - Analytics will start collecting data after deployment

3. **Verify Installation**
   - After deployment, visit your site
   - Open browser DevTools > Network tab
   - Look for requests to `/_vercel/insights/view`
   - Check the Analytics dashboard after a few user visits

## Technical Notes

- The Analytics component is lightweight and loads asynchronously
- It only sends data when deployed to Vercel (no local tracking)
- Privacy-focused: collects only anonymous pageview data by default
- No additional configuration required for basic web analytics
- For custom events, upgrade to Vercel Pro or Enterprise plans

